Review the uncommitted stmap54 implementation for correctness and campaign-policy issues.

Context:
- stmap54 is iteration 54 in the stmap family.
- It clones the stmap53 two-pass SCL load feedback command and uses mapper mode 55.
- The intended source change is a cut-only one-sided severe-pressure exception: keep the reviewed stmap53 pressure-agreement/pressure-near behavior intact, but in mode 55 admit only candidates with missing node pressure, bounded cut pressure, severe feedback, measured sink-pressure entries >= 8000, and stronger mapper-arrival gain.
- Existing map and stmap0 through stmap53 behavior must remain unchanged.

Please prioritize:
- correctness bugs, memory lifetime bugs, mode gating mistakes, or parser/logging issues that would invalidate evaluation;
- accidental behavior changes to existing commands or mapper modes;
- missing validation artifacts or required runtime records.

Validation already run:
- make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1
- ./abc -c "stmap54 -h"
- smoke flow on benchmarks/i10.aig
- full baseline/candidate flows on i10, ode, or1200, syn2
- CEC for all four required benchmarks

Return findings only, with severity and file/line references. If no actionable findings, say so.

codex
The new mode 55 omits the stmap53 pressure-near exception path it is intended to preserve, so stmap54 behavior is not a strict extension of the reviewed stmap53 branch.

Review comment:

- [P2] Preserve stmap53 pressure-near path in mode 55 — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:1602-1602
  When a mode-55 candidate satisfies the reviewed stmap53 pressure-near exception (severe feedback, sufficient sink-pressure entries, both pressure sides present/bounded/near) but does not have pressure agreement and is not the new cut-only case, this path falls back to `Map_MatchStmap52ModeratePenaltyFactor()` and never evaluates `Map_MatchStmap53HasPressureNearException()`. That makes stmap54 block candidates that stmap53 would admit, so it is not adding the cut-only exception on top of the reviewed stmap53 behavior.
